    "number": 72,
    "summary": "1–8, Elders are to render an account of their stewardship unto the bishop; 9–15, The bishop keeps the storehouse and cares for the poor and needy; 16–26, Bishops are to certify the worthiness of elders.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [
      {
        "type": "introduction",
        "text": "Revelation given through Joseph Smith the Prophet, at Kirtland, Ohio, December 4, 1831. Several elders and members had assembled to learn their duty and to be further edified in the teachings of the Church. This section is a compilation of three revelations received on the same day.Verses 1 through 8make known the calling of Newel K. Whitney as a bishop. He was then called and ordained, after whichverses 9 through 23were received, giving additional information as to a bishop’s duties. Thereafter,verses 24 through 26were given, providing instructions concerning the gathering to Zion."
      }
    ],
    "verses": [
      {
